From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:40:22 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-msm8996: keep PCIe GDSCs in retention during
 suspend

The PCIe controller keeps its resources on during system suspend when a
device is linked up, but genpd switches the controller's power domain off
in the noirq phase. On resume the link is gone: the endpoint reads back
as inaccessible ("Unable to change power state from D3hot to D0") and the
next access hangs the bus.

Seen with the QCA6174 Wi-Fi on PCIe0 of a Samsung Galaxy Tab S3 in
s2idle: the tablet resets during resume.

Use PWRSTS_RET_ON for the PCIe GDSCs, like the PCIe GDSCs of newer SoCs
(sm8250 and others): a power-off then leaves them on and lets the
hardware put them in retention.

Signed-off-by: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8996.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8996.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8996.c
index aa3bd27778..dc8b6f3f3d 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8996.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8996.c
@@ -3239,7 +3239,7 @@ static struct gdsc pcie0_gdsc = {
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "pcie0",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
 };
 
 static struct gdsc pcie1_gdsc = {
@@ -3247,7 +3247,7 @@ static struct gdsc pcie1_gdsc = {
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "pcie1",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
 };
 
 static struct gdsc pcie2_gdsc = {
@@ -3255,7 +3255,7 @@ static struct gdsc pcie2_gdsc = {
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "pcie2",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
 };
 
 static struct gdsc ufs_gdsc = {
